        "id": 129135,
        "name": "Killswitch",
        "username": "Killswitch",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/killswitch/{size}/2116_2.png",
        "created_at": "2015-01-23T20:19:54.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>What specifically are you confused about?</p><p>Basically, at the start of each of his turns, count how many of his cards are in play that have \"Manifestation\" in the orange box beneath the card art. Examples of Manifestations are Ocular Swarm, Twisted Miscreation, and Lambent Reaper. So, if you have H or more of these in play, you flip his cards to reveal the other side, the Unstable Despoiler. And just a note here, \"H\" represents the number of heroes you are taking into the fight. So if you use Sky-Scraper, Guise and Captain Cosmic, \"H\" equals 3.</p><p>If you reveal Insanity B with Insanity A, insanity A only plays B, and nothing else happens, because it is a one-shot. However, if Insanity B reveals a manifestation, you copy only Insanity B again.</p>",
        "post_number": 2,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:04:01.334Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
